From: OpenCanon contributors
Date: 2026-11-04
Subject: Allocate a complete NULL sentinel for buffered image row pointers
License: GPL-2.0-or-later

Gutenprint 5.3.4 Debian orig source, corresponding to package
5.3.4.20220624T01008808d602-1. The cleanup loop reads height + 1
pointers, so adding one byte per row does not reserve a sentinel for
short images. Keep all original pixels and fix the allocation itself.

--- a/src/main/buffer-image.c
+++ b/src/main/buffer-image.c
@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@
 	int i;
 	/* fill buffer */
 	if(!priv->buf){
-		priv->buf = stp_zalloc((sizeof(unsigned short*) + 1) * height);
+		priv->buf = stp_zalloc(sizeof(*priv->buf) * ((size_t)height + 1));
 		if(!priv->buf){
 			return STP_IMAGE_STATUS_ABORT;
 		}
